What are Printed Circuit Boards?
Printed Circuit Boards (PCBs) serve as the backbone of modern electronics, providing both mechanical support and electrical connectivity through conductive copper traces laminated onto non-conductive substrates. These vital components exist in several configurations—single-sided, double-sided, and multi-layer rigid boards alongside flexible and rigid-flex variants—to accommodate diverse application requirements across industries.
