Competitive Landscape
The global PCB market features a mix of large-scale Asian manufacturers and specialized Western producers, with competitive dynamics varying significantly by product segment:
Asian Powerhouses
Chinese manufacturers like Shennan Circuits and Aoshikang dominate volume production, while Japanese/Korean firms (Ibiden, SEMCO) lead in high-end IC substrates and advanced packaging solutions. Taiwanese players (Unimicron, Tripod) excel in flexible circuits and mid-range multilayer boards.
Western Specialists
Companies like TTM Technologies and AT&S focus on aerospace, defense, and automotive sectors, differentiating through rapid prototyping capabilities and specialized manufacturing techniques.
